WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:00.660
Hello everybody!

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:03.740
My name is Markiplier and welcome back to Subnautica.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.380
Now, I finally,

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.600
FINALLY,

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.240
finished construction of my castle,

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.120
on the island.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.340
And it may not seem like much,

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.020
it may not seem like I've done all that much from last time.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:20.420
But let me tell you, I've worked way too long to try to get this thing in

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.620
GLORIOUS, WORKING ORDER.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.800
As you can see, power is no longer a problem.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.140
I've got UNLIMITED power panels supplying my spotlights,

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.180
which hopefully will allow me to be rescued!

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.820
At some point in my life, they're gonna come...

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.220
and... help me...

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.760
when I'm alone... on this island...

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.440
But until that day comes, I have to entertain myself.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.260
So please!

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.260
Come on into my home!

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.560
As you can see,

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.800
remember how the plants wanted to be in my base anyway?

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.480
I just kinda rolled with it.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.280
Because if they're gonna be in here,

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.300
I might as well fill the rest of it in!

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.940
I've got plants on the walls,

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.360
plants in the pots,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.040
plants in the garden,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.700
I've got lots and lots of hanging fruit tree,

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:05.600
I never,

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:06.320
ever,

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:07.480
EVER

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.580
need to worry about food again.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.960
I've got so much food!

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:14.220
Endless amounts of food!

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.720
Perfect for going exploring in a giant empty ocean that is my life!

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:19.980
So...

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.820
as we move up through the different levels, you'll see.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:26.920
Just in case I don't wanna go into the ocean to find my fish friends,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.340
who just so happen to be my only friends...

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.680
and the only ones that'll keep me warm at night...

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.440
[expression of crushing loneliness]

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:34.680
... I keep 'em here!

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.080
In my aquarium,

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:39.300
is where I just look at them and watch them as they

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.820
wallow in misery

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:42.580
at their isolation from their home.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.020
Because that's something that we can relate on.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.280
Our crushing loneliness.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.280
Now, speaking of crushing loneliness,

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:52.680
in the next room, we have what I call 'The Friendship Room'!

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.320
Every time I make a new friend on this island,

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.700
I'm gonna put their picture on the wall, and then...

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:00.440
make sure they sit in the chair!

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:01.740
Forever!

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.580
So that we can hang out and laugh and laugh

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.240
[empty echoes] and laugh and laugh...

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.500
It'll happen eventually.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:08.720
Someday!

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:10.780
Someday!

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:13.700
Okay. And in the next room, we have the fabrication stuff.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.420
Because when you have a lot of friends,

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.560
and we're all moving in and outta the house, eating all my food,

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.780
laughing at all my jokes, hanging out with me,

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.780
sharing a bed together...

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.220
Y'know, it- [stammers]

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.080
You don't wanna crowd one fabricator,

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.860
I'm planning for the future here!

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.900
So, plenty of stuff to be used here.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.920
Now, this is-this is my thinking room.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.460
I like to, I like to keep this one generally,

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.600
very isolated from the other rooms because-

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.620
a-a-and it's pretty barebones, because

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:41.160
when I'm thinking of this room,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.640
ah, I don't really have anything other than my own thoughts to keep me company?

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.720
So I just like to keep it the way it is.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.380
And then I go up to the next room,

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.600
which is another one of my friendship rooms!

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.360
And speaking of which, it's nothing but lockers.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.920
So I have new names to put on the lockers.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.220
Which are over there!

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.380
I can't see it!

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:01.740
WHERE IS IT?

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:06.500
Okay! So the first name going on the brand new lockers directly away

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.160
from the ladder, if I was going up there...

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:11.880
The first one goes to Rainbow Chipmunk, so.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.020
'RNBW CHPMK'.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.040
There we go! Good enough!

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:17.900
Who said:

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.580
"Wow Mark, that's the most planning you've ever done."

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:21.540
And I had to look!

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:24.460
And all I did was talk about a potted plant.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.540
So, thank you for having so much faith in me and low expectations.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.440
I have the same things about myself.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.880
And the next one goes to

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.760
Jill K

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:34.940
Who commented that

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.020
in every game that I ever play in,

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.760
I am my own worst enemy.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:39.820
That and doorways.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.300
So, thank you very much.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.140
And then, Jay Pyris...

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:44.980
Jay Pris-

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:47.080
Py-Pyre, Pyris

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.320
Who reminded me

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:49.640
that even though I don't have Wilson

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.600
companioning m-m-me me,

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.120
I have Karen.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.380
My computer wife

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.760
who's going to be with me

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.480
throughout all eternity

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.620
in my solitude on this island.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:02.120
[dying on the inside]

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:03.100
Anyway!

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:04.920
Also, Connor Marks

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.280
So, 'Cnnr Mrk'

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.560
um, who said:

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.680
"Markiplier, can you find the Lifepod wrecks?"

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.160
Which is actually something that I wanna do.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.480
And I have a list here.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:15.880
Because there e-eh

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:18.460
many of you have asked yourself throughout this game:

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.880
"Why aren't there any other survivors?"

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:22.620
And the fact of the matter is...

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:23.860
there were.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:26.340
There were other jettisoned lifepods,

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.320
but as you can see,

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.460
when coming into the atmosphere for some reason,

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.660
they all blew up. Even mine did!

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.900
Mine blew up and I was able to put out the fire.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.600
I got knocked out right in the head!

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.220
But I was able to put out the fire.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:38.060
Oh! By the way!

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.140
That's a new intro sequence that you guys haven't seen yet.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.460
Let me play that right now for ya!

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:42.420
It's really cool, so-

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:43.160
Bing!

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.840
Computer: Power failure - Imminent.

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:48.180
[Alarm blaring]
Computer: All personnel, abandon ship.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.700
[Heavy panting]

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.340
[Grunt]

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:53.940
[Distant explosion, rumbling]

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:57.240
Computer: Launching in 3, 2, 1...

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:58.920
[Rockets firing]

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:08.420
[Rumbling explosion]

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:12.820
[Metal clanking]

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:17.740
[Beeping]

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.480
Guh! Anyway.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:20.980
So, that's not good.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:23.160
So now, the game actually does start-

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.020
I'm just gonna roll into this 'cause, whatever.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:25.700
Alright.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:27.960
Awe- thumping bass.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.420
Alright, so then you pick up this,

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.560
put out the fire,

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:35.040
first spray it up to the left because you feel like it and you're a badass,

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.220
herbaderbaderba

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:38.040
Pretty cool right?

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.580
So when you start a new game in Subnautica, that's what you see

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:42.720
and it kinda gives an explanation of the panic

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:43.600
coming outta there

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:47.520
and just imagine other lifepods that were leaving the ship as well,

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.520
but they didn't make it.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.040
And we're gonna go to them,

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:52.460
but I have just a few more things to show you

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:54.000
in my lovely home.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.920
My castle on an island!

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:57.860
All by myself!

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:02.520
So, this is the top floor and obviously there's not a lot going on here.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:06.080
It became harder and harder to build out as I went farther up.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.440
But over here...

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:09.220
I have another aquarium!

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:11.440
And these are called 'Holefish'.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:12.800
As you can see,

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:15.540
they're so- [awkward laughter]

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.940
Oh my god, are they all dead? Holy shit, that's horrifying!

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.120
They weren't like that when I first put them in there,

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:21.800
but...

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.540
they look very dead.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:26.600
But the reason that I filled it with exclusively holefish

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:27.720
is because...

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.220
much like me,

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:32.600
they have a hole inside them that can never be filled.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.620
[Dead inside] So there you go...

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:37.320
Anyway!

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:38.740
And the final thing,

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:41.940
the coup de grace of this entire castle

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:44.240
is my observation chamber

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:49.940
where I can sit in this chair and watch the moon go by.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:55.280
If you can even call that a moon, because there's a separate thing that's actually also a moon here,

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.840
that's just another planet that's orbiting-

00:06:57.840 --> 00:06:58.660
Ah, there it is!

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:02.180
It's kind of a weird double moon situation, that's actually really pretty.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.480
Look at that!

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.000
Look at that!

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.360
And that is actually- they're not fooling anybody.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:09.300
I think that's Earth's moon there.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:11.080
Just judging by the graphic of it.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:11.960
But anyway.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:13.960
So that is my castle,

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:17.240
the crushing loneliness eats away at me at the darkest of nights-

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.040
Ignore that, I wasn't done building.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.360
[cough] Anyway, so.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:26.340
The next thing that we're gonna do, is we're actually going to go to these ship pods.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.640
But I'm gonna wait until daytime

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:30.340
because it's going to suck to be in the middle of the ocean at night

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.100
and I need to get my, uh, Seamoth anyway.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:35.160
So I need to go back down to my water base,

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:38.120
where my Seamoth is conveniently stored~

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.000
I'mma take a few of these for the road.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.480
Just in case...

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:44.860
Aw, isn't that a lovely lightshow? See?

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:46.600
No one could miss this!

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:51.180
If anyone was flying by in a nearby galaxy, it's a party!

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:53.540
They know someone has fun here!

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:55.440
BY THEMSELF.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.400
(noises of loneliness)

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:00.040
Hup!
Computer: Welcome aboard, captain.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:04.220
Thank you Karen, I've missed you. Hope you've been good.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:09.320
I'm going to go on an adventure to find the corpses of my fallen comrades.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:11.000
Oh I forgot. I forgot another way.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.300
But there's a weird thing here. Uh, if I go down one...

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:16.040
Um...

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:21.260
For some reason the ocean doesn't quite clear out on this level but it just transitions down here

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:25.660
and then it's air again, for some bizarre reason. I have no idea why that is that way.

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:29.720
So, now I got my Seamoth, and now I'm gonna go with the "F**K A DUCK"

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:32.560
and we're gonna go find us some caves.

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:36.760
But to be a little bit easier, I'm just gonna use warp commands because I would have to like,

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:43.960
finaglely find them, and I don't wanna do that because even though they're in generally easy-to-find areas

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:47.820
I'm going to show you exactly where they are. Right now.

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:49.200
Well, that didn't work.

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:50.740
Why didn't that work?

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:53.480
Can I not be in my Seamoth when I do that?

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:54.760
Let me try that without...

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.500
It's gonna suck without. But...

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:58.080
I don't even have my...

00:08:58.920 --> 00:08:59.760
Ehhh, I can make it.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:00.520
Ooh.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:06.620
Whoa, whoA, whOA, wHOA, WHOA, whoa, whoa... cool.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:09.720
Alright, so it's gotta be around here- *scary angry fish noise*

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:11.560
I forgot, you're here.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.100
Oh hey buddy, don't- don't even think about it bro!

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:18.860
Don't- don't- don't- don't- no, no, noot, noot, noot, noot-

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:20.680
That's right, you better back off, okay.

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:22.160
So just about...

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:23.760
Where are we looking at here?

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.960
Oh god, I'm out of air. I forgot my airtank!

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.880
OOOOH SHIT.
Computer: Emergency, 10 seconds of oxygen remaining.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:28.440
Oh god.

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:29.480
Oh god.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:30.300
Oh god.

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:32.180
I fucked up, I fucked up.

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:33.400
Where was it?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.500
I was supposed to have spawned right on top of it-

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:36.640
(gasps of realizations/air needed)

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:40.020
Oh no, is that one of the new features that's not in my game?

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:41.780
(human breaching noise of sorts)

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:45.140
Just barely made right at the crack of dawn. Thank you very much.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:49.920
See, the unfortunate thing is that the next time that I play this game, I actually-

00:09:51.140 --> 00:09:52.660
Oh, it's not here, is it?

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:55.120
Oh my god, it's not.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:57.060
Aw, dangit!

00:09:58.020 --> 00:09:58.980
Is it not here?

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:04.600
Awww crap. Okay, so I was wondering what was going on.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:09.760
See, the thing is: I've been playing this one saved game for so long,

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:13.960
that I actually- see, I- yeah I would've found that immediately, that's my original base.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.460
Like, that's my base there.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:19.600
If it was here, I would've found it. So what happened is,

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:25.200
I've been playing this particular game for so long, and they've done so many updates to the game,

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:30.960
that the terrain- they've upgraded my saved game but I've actually been excluded from some of the more

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:35.280
pertinent things in the game. So, I'm gonna start a new game, here real quick...

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.520
and then I'm gonna show you these things.

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:38.320
I'm not gonna NOT show you these things.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:40.220
I've gotta show you these things.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:46.000
Okay so we're back. This is now the "experimental mode", which has new "epdates-"

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:46.680
Euuuughhh-

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:51.420
New updates coming out for the game every few days, instead of waiting for about a month

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:57.400
in between each one. So this means that saved games get invalid all the time, but this means also

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:01.740
that new features get put out as they're made, and they're made all the time.

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:02.980
So, with that-

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:05.720
Computer: -detecting increased local radiation levels-

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:06.320
NOOO-

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:11.280
So, the reason why we're here is we're gonna find these escape pods, which is going to be dangerous

00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:15.080
cause I don't have much air, but that doesn't matter cause we're gonna be fine. Alright.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:15.800
So.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:20.640
Warping to the first one, and as you'll see when we get here- whoopise doopsie.

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:22.480
I can't see shit. There we go.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:29.980
